  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a permutation PPP, we define f(P)f(P)f(P) to be it's prefix max array, i.e. f(P)i=max⁡(P1,P2,…,Pi)f(P)_i = \\max(P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_i)f(P)i​=max(P1​,P2​,…,Pi​).\n\nNow, you are given a partially filled in permutation PPP of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N], i.e. some elements are −1-1−1. You want to replace the −1-1−1 elements with integers in [1,N][1, N][1,N] to make it a permutation.\n\nWhat are the total number of distinct f(P)f(P)f(P) possible? Since the answer may be large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of possible values of f(P)f(P)f(P) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤50002 \\le N \\le 50002≤N≤5000",
      "Pi=−1P_i = -1Pi​=−1 or 1≤Pi≤N1 \\le P_i \\le N1≤Pi​≤N",
      "All the non −1-1−1 values in PPP are distinct.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500050005000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n3\n-1 -1 -1\n3\n1 2 3\n4\n2 -1 3 -1\n4\n-1 -1 2 -1\n8\n-1 -1 1 -1 -1 5 -1 -1",
        "output": "5\n1\n2\n5\n132",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : All 666 permutations of N=3N = 3N=3 are possible. But [3,1,2][3, 1, 2][3,1,2] and [3,2,1][3, 2, 1][3,2,1] form the same prefix maximum array, and hence there are only 555 distinct prefix maximum arrays possible."
      }
    ]
